(FIL-50: Read line reads up to a newline or EOF and INCLUDES the trailing newline when one is present; the final line of a file with no trailing newline is returned whole.
 Also covers: FIL-52, FIL-53.
 "one\n" is 4 bytes - 3 characters plus the newline the manual says is kept.
 "tail-without-newline" is 20 bytes with no newline to keep.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-50.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   4
   one
  
   20
   tail-without-newline
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/noeol.txt".
Write "one\ntail-without-newline" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
open a file for reading called source at "vf_scratch/files/noeol.txt".
a buffer called linebuf is 64 bytes in size.
Read line from source into linebuf.
print linebuf's size.
print linebuf.
Read line from source into linebuf.
print linebuf's size.
print linebuf.
Close source.
